## 3. Bible texts — status varies by text

`versions.json` carries a `year`, `base_text` and `note` for each version and is
the best starting point for working out the status of any one file.

**Public domain by age (verified licence statement at source):** Wycliffe (1395),
Tyndale New Testament (1526), Geneva Bible (1599), Leeser Old Testament (1853),
Targum Onkelos / Etheridge (1862), Noyes Translation (1869), KJV Cambridge
Paragraph Bible (1873), Darby Bible (1890), Bible in Basic English, and the
long-standing public-domain texts already in the corpus (KJV, ASV, YLT,
Douay-Rheims, Webster, JPS 1917, Brenton, the Greek and Hebrew source editions,
the Clementine Vulgate, and the older non-English versions).

**Public domain by age of the underlying text, digital edition's licence not
individually verified:** Samaritan Pentateuch, Syriac Peshitta, Vulgata Sixtina
(1590), Gothic Bible / Wulfila (c. 350), Rotherham Emphasised Bible (1902),
Twentieth Century New Testament (1904). The texts themselves are far out of
copyright; the transcriptions were obtained via
[scrollmapper/bible_databases](https://github.com/scrollmapper/bible_databases).

**Licence not verified:** `versions/he/MIQRA AL PI HAMESORAH` is a *modern*
(2013) critical edition, so age does not put it in the public domain. Confirm its
terms before redistributing it specifically.

---

## 4. Modern translations under active copyright — read this before redistributing

**This repository contains complete texts of modern English translations that are
under active copyright and are not licensed by this file.** They predate the
lexicon and research work and no permission or licensing arrangement for them is
recorded anywhere in the repository.

At minimum the following appear to fall in this category:

> Amplified Bible · Aramaic Bible in Plain English · Berean Standard Bible ·
> Christian Standard Bible · Contemporary English Version · English Standard
> Version · God's Word Translation · Good News Translation · Holman Christian
> Standard Bible · International Standard Version · Legacy Standard Bible ·
> Literal Standard Version · Majority Standard Bible · NASB 1977 · NASB 1995 ·
> NET Bible · New American Bible · New American Standard Bible · New Heart English
> Bible · New International Version · New King James Version · New Living
> Translation · New Revised Standard Version · Peshitta Holy Bible Translated
>
> …and the Contemporary English Version, Good News Translation, New American Bible
> and New Revised Standard Version files under `apocrypha-versions/`.

Most publishers permit limited quotation without written permission — typically a
few hundred to a thousand verses, not exceeding a stated fraction of the work, and
not a whole book. Redistributing a complete text goes well beyond that. Anyone
relying on this repository, and the repository owner, should treat these files as
a question to resolve rather than a settled permission.

This section is a factual note about what the repository contains. It grants no
rights and is not a determination of infringement.

---

## 5. Not legal advice

This file records the provenance and stated terms of the material as far as they
could be established from the sources, and it is written by the repository's
contributors, not by a lawyer. It is a starting point for doing your own
diligence, not a substitute for it. Where a source's own licence statement
conflicts with anything here, **the source's statement governs.**
